    "result_text": "Build is green with the tests passing.\n\n## What I changed\n\nI agreed with the finding \u2014 the SHA-256\u2192hex plumbing was duplicated between `Owner.sha256LowerHex` and `ClinicServiceImpl.sha256UpperHex`, and putting `MessageDigest`/checked-exception handling into the JPA entity broke the codebase's `util`-package convention that this very change reinforced with `Soundex`.\n\nFix:\n- **Added `util/Sha256Hex.java`** with `lowerHex(value)` (full 64-char lower-case) and `upperHex(value, chars)` (truncated upper-case), sharing one `digest()` + `hex()` implementation.\n- **`Owner.getIdentityKey()`** now delegates to `Sha256Hex.lowerHex(...)`; removed the private `sha256LowerHex` and the `MessageDigest`/`StandardCharsets`/`NoSuchAlgorithmException` imports from the entity.\n- **`ClinicServiceImpl`** now calls `Sha256Hex.upperHex(...)` from both `generateCustomerCode` and `generateHouseholdId`; removed the private `sha256UpperHex` and its crypto imports.\n\nNo behavioural change \u2014 `upperHex` preserves the existing truncation semantics (customer-code hash 8 chars, household id 12 chars), and the identity key is still the full lower-case digest. All acceptance behaviour is intact and the suite is green.",
